[{:db/id 17592186133628 :question/problem "If ![](images/4b/4baf2c746763156bd576054a684a92313185323f40b0dd4c54d4ba29650481aa.svg) ![](images/f1/f1dc50e7cc723ff619fa0ccf3f155c65161a3e6c640385c3b4a5c19f3d66741a.svg) and $\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = 34,$ then what is $\\dfrac{\\mathbf{u}\\cdot 2\\mathbf{v}}{3\\mathbf{v}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133757 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5008b167-e8a9-508a-9bad-146a4857fbba"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133758 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-34e8f50c-adbf-51d4-b0d4-a2150385ab67"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133567 :question/problem "Suppose $(4\\mathbf{a} + 2\\mathbf{b}) \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = {0},$ where $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{0}.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = -2(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{a})$\n\nII. $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} =  0$\n\nIII. $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = 1$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5008b167-e8a9-508a-9bad-146a4857fbba" :question/id #uuid "5008b167-e8a9-508a-9bad-146a4857fbba" :question/math-academy-id "q-74045" :question/problem "Suppose ${b}_{2}=q{b}_{1}+a$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2}=-4.$ If $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and ${b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$, find the value of $q.$ \n\n*Hint: You might wish to take the equation ${b}_{2}=q{b}_{1}+a$ and find the dot product of both sides with ${b}_{1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the equation ${b}_{2}=q{b}_{1}+a$ and find the dot product of both sides with ${b}_{1}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} & =q{b}_{1}+a \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & ={b}_{1}\\cdot (q{b}_{1}+a) \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & ={b}_{1}\\cdot (q{b}_{1})+({b}_{1}\\cdot a) \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & =q({b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1})+({b}_{1}\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the formula for the dot product to compute the values of ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1} & ={b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\  & =9+16 \\\\  & =25 \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot a & ={b}_{1}{a}_{1}+{b}_{2}{a}_{2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3+8 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the values for ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1},$ ${b}_{1}\\cdot a,$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & =q({b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1})+({b}_{1}\\cdot a) \\\\ -4 & =q\\cdot 25+11 \\\\ -25q & =15 \\\\ q & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cb20dfa1-3b66-5467-a387-ca9ce4c4fd61"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb20dfa1-3b66-5467-a387-ca9ce4c4fd61" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb20dfa1-3b66-5467-a387-ca9ce4c4fd61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0ff61a3d-11e1-5c24-a4c0-eb5c2f727280" :answer-field/choices ["answer-105fb53f-a973-5605-818d-1c2b476234cd" "answer-0ff61a3d-11e1-5c24-a4c0-eb5c2f727280" "answer-fa68821a-605f-5327-b1d5-cc2363ae0488" "answer-7545ce1c-fbdd-52ac-ac9c-cfeceb2c4411" "answer-aad07bb7-3639-5c8d-96b9-7f614d3b5f47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-105fb53f-a973-5605-818d-1c2b476234cd" :answer/id #uuid "105fb53f-a973-5605-818d-1c2b476234cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ff61a3d-11e1-5c24-a4c0-eb5c2f727280" :answer/id #uuid "0ff61a3d-11e1-5c24-a4c0-eb5c2f727280" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa68821a-605f-5327-b1d5-cc2363ae0488" :answer/id #uuid "fa68821a-605f-5327-b1d5-cc2363ae0488" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7545ce1c-fbdd-52ac-ac9c-cfeceb2c4411" :answer/id #uuid "7545ce1c-fbdd-52ac-ac9c-cfeceb2c4411" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aad07bb7-3639-5c8d-96b9-7f614d3b5f47" :answer/id #uuid "aad07bb7-3639-5c8d-96b9-7f614d3b5f47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-34e8f50c-adbf-51d4-b0d4-a2150385ab67" :question/id #uuid "34e8f50c-adbf-51d4-b0d4-a2150385ab67" :question/math-academy-id "q-39207" :question/problem "Suppose $(4a+2b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $a\\cdot a<0$\n\nII. $b\\cdot a=\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nIII. $b\\cdot a=-2(a\\cdot a)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $a\\ne 0,$ we must have $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement II is false since it leads to a contradiction. If $b\\cdot a=\\frac{1}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 4(a\\cdot a)+2(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 4(a\\cdot a)+2(\\frac{1}{2}) & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a & =-\\frac{1}{4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut this is a contradiction since $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Simplifying the expression $(4a+2b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ (4a)\\cdot a+(2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 4(a\\cdot a)+2(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 2(b\\cdot a) & =-4(a\\cdot a) \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-2(a\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-612fca8f-e7e8-5291-ad03-38fa3749ba41"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-612fca8f-e7e8-5291-ad03-38fa3749ba41" :answer-field/id #uuid "612fca8f-e7e8-5291-ad03-38fa3749ba41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-09065806-b133-53e7-a415-f60daab53b99" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8aef25aa-ccf6-5e00-8e61-47a0af94462a" "answer-71b3b29c-1c8b-59df-b6b7-57376201da06" "answer-650f79ed-8cca-54b7-b878-11eaac10aaa0" "answer-201f2230-7957-57ee-9f4c-64a64340bee2" "answer-09065806-b133-53e7-a415-f60daab53b99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8aef25aa-ccf6-5e00-8e61-47a0af94462a" :answer/id #uuid "8aef25aa-ccf6-5e00-8e61-47a0af94462a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71b3b29c-1c8b-59df-b6b7-57376201da06" :answer/id #uuid "71b3b29c-1c8b-59df-b6b7-57376201da06" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-650f79ed-8cca-54b7-b878-11eaac10aaa0" :answer/id #uuid "650f79ed-8cca-54b7-b878-11eaac10aaa0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-201f2230-7957-57ee-9f4c-64a64340bee2" :answer/id #uuid "201f2230-7957-57ee-9f4c-64a64340bee2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09065806-b133-53e7-a415-f60daab53b99" :answer/id #uuid "09065806-b133-53e7-a415-f60daab53b99" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186342140 :question/problem "Suppose $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $a\\cdot a=0$\n\nII. $a\\cdot b>0$\n\nIII. $a\\cdot b<0$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135029 :tutorial/content "Recall that for two vectors $\\mathbf{u}, \\mathbf{v} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n,$ the **dot product** is defined as the sum of products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =[\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} \\\\ {u}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {u}_{n}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {v}_{n}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+⋯+{u}_{n}\\cdot {v}_{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{u}_{i}{v}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133981 :activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
